14. VERY IMPORTANT: ARRAY PARAMETER
------------------------------------------------------------

Consider:

void display(int arr[])
{
    printf("%zu\n", sizeof(arr));
}

Inside this function parameter, `arr` is adjusted to a pointer.

Therefore:

sizeof(arr)

is the size of a pointer, NOT the size of the original array.


Correct approach:

