============================================================
              MOST IMPORTANT INTERVIEW POINTS
============================================================

Remember these extremely well:

1. Array indexing starts at 0.

2. For N elements:

       valid indexes = 0 ... N-1

3. Array elements are contiguous.

4. Array access by index is O(1).

5. In most expressions, an array converts to pointer to its
   first element.

6. sizeof(array) gives total array size only when the object
   is actually an array in that scope.

7. Function array parameters are adjusted to pointers.

8. C does not automatically perform array bounds checking.

9. Out-of-bounds access is undefined behavior.

10. `int *p[5]` = array of pointers.

11. `int (*p)[5]` = pointer to array.

12. `arr[i]` is equivalent to `*(arr + i)`.

13. `&arr[0]` and `arr` point to the first element in the
    relevant expressions.

14. `&arr` points to the entire array and has a different type.

15. C strings require a terminating `'\0'`.

16. A function cannot directly return an array type.

17. Dynamic arrays can be implemented using malloc/realloc/free.

18. Always consider memory bounds and allocation overflow.

19. C arrays do not carry their length as part of the array
    object in ordinary function parameters.

20. Array + pointer concepts are fundamental to advanced C.


